  "verbalization": "Calenduloside C appears to interact with DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular targets, with the most direct link being its interaction with VMRC-LCP. This suggests that Calenduloside C may act as a modulator or inhibitor of VMRC-LCP, which in turn targets DNA polymerase iota. The evidence is consistent across three paths, with all three linking Calenduloside C to DNA polymerase iota via VMRC-LCP or a complex, long-chain compound that also targets DNA polymerase iota. The presence of multiple targets, including both a short-chain and a long-chain compound, indicates a potential dual mechanism of action. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that Calenduloside C may influence DNA polymerase iota through a series of intermediate targets, possibly by modulating the activity of VMRC-LCP or by directly interacting with the enzyme. The evidence supports a role for Calenduloside C in regulating DNA polymerase iota, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
